n><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> instance[j]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">                marginal </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> model_predict(with_i) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> model_predict(without_i)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">                weight </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (np.math.factorial(</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">len</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(subset)) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">*</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">                         np.math.factorial(n_features </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> len</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(subset) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">                         np.math.factorial(n_features))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">                marginal_contributions.append(weight </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">*</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> marginal)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">        shapley_values[i] </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(marginal_contributions)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    return</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> shapley_values</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">def</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> simple_model</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(x):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    return</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 3</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> *</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> x[</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">] </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> *</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> x[</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">] </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> x[</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">] </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 5</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">instance </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> np.array([</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1.0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2.0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">3.0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">baseline </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> np.array([</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0.0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0.0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0.0</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">sv </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> exact_shapley(simple_model, instance, instance, baseline)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">print</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">f</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Prediction: </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">{</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">simple_model(instance)</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">}</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">print</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">f</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Baseline: </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">{</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">simple_model(baseline)</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">}</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">print</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">f</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"SHAP values: </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">{</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">sv</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">}</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">print</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">f</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Sum of SHAP: </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">{sum</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(sv)</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">:.1f</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">}</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> (should = </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">{</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">simple_model(instance) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> simple_model(baseline)</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">:.1f</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">}</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">)\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span></code></pre></div><p><strong>TreeSHAP</strong>是针对树模型（GBDT、Random Forest）的高效 SHAP 计算算法，将复杂度从 O(2ⁿ) 降低到 O(TLD²)（T=树数量，L=叶子数，D=深度）。<strong>KernelSHAP</strong>是模型无关的 SHAP 近似算法，通过加权线性回归来近似 Shapley 值。</p>\n<h2 id=\"lime-与反事实解释\">LIME 与反事实解释</h2><p>**LIME（Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations）**通过在预测点附近生成扰动样本，训练一个局部的可解释模型（通常是加权线性回归）来解释黑箱模型的局部行为。LIME 的优势是对任何模型都适用且解释直观，局限是局部解释可能不稳定（对扰动方式和邻域大小敏感）。</p>\n<p>**反事实解释（Counterfactual Explanations）**回答&quot;如果输入发生什么变化，预测结果会改变？&quot;这类问题。例如：在贷款被拒的场景中，反事实解释可能说&quot;如果您的年收入增加 20% 或还清现有贷款的 50%，贷款将被批准&quot;。反事实解释的价值在于它直接提供了可操作的改进建议。</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"graph\" data-source=\"graph LR&#10;    subgraph 解释方法适用场景&#10;        A[模型审计] --&gt; B[SHAP 全局特征重要性]&#10;        C[个体决策解释] --&gt; D[LIME / SHAP 局部]&#10;        E[用户可操作建议] --&gt; F[反事实解释]&#10;        G[模型调试] --&gt; H[PDP / ICE 图]&#10;        I[合规文档] --&gt; J[规则提取 / 全局代理模型]&#10;    end\">graph LR\n    subgraph 解释方法适用场景\n        A[模型审计] --&gt; B[SHAP 全局特征重要性]\n        C[个体决策解释] --&gt; D[LIME / SHAP 局部]\n        E[用户可操作建议] --&gt; F[反事实解释]\n        G[模型调试] --&gt; H[PDP / ICE 图]\n        I[合规文档] --&gt; J[规则提取 / 全局代理模型]\n    end</pre><h2 id=\"可解释性与性能的权衡\">可解释性与性能的权衡</h2><p>可解释性和模型性能之间的权衡是实践中最核心的决策之一。</p>\n<p><strong>事前可解释模型</strong>（线性回归、逻辑回归、决策树、GAM）天然具有可解释性，但在复杂非线性问题上的预测性能通常不如深度学习。**EBM（Explainable Boosting Machine）**是 Microsoft Research 提出的 GAM+交互项模型，在多个表格数据基准测试中达到了接近 XGBoost 的性能，同时保持了完全的可解释性。</p>\n<p><strong>事后解释的可靠性</strong>是一个活跃的研究问题。多项研究表明，LIME 和 SHAP 的解释在某些情况下可能不稳定或误导——相似的输入可能产生截然不同的解释，且解释可能被对抗性地操纵（即模型在重要特征上的行为可以被故意隐藏）。</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>模型选择</th>\n<th>可解释性</th>\n<th>性能</th>\n<th>适用场景</th>\n<th>合规要求</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>线性/逻辑回归</td>\n<td>最高</td>\n<td>低</td>\n<td>低维/线性关系</td>\n<td>高风险场景首选</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GAM/EBM</td>\n<td>高</td>\n<td>中高</td>\n<td>表格数据</td>\n<td>高风险+性能需求</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GBDT + SHAP</td>\n<td>中（事后）</td>\n<td>高</td>\n<td>通用表格数据</td>\n<td>中等风险</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DNN + LIME</td>\n<td>低（事后）</td>\n<td>最高</td>\n<td>图像/NLP</td>\n<td>低风险/内部使用</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>可解释 AI 是合规（GDPR Art. 22）、信任构建和模型调试的三重需求</li>\n<li>SHAP 基于 Shapley 值理论，是唯一满足四个公平分配公理的加性特征归因方法</li>\n<li>LIME 提供模型无关的局部解释，反事实解释提供用户可操作的改进建议</li>\n<li>EBM（可解释增强机）在表格数据上达到接近 GBDT 的性能同时保持完全可解释性</li>\n<li>事后解释方法（LIME/SHAP）的稳定性和可靠性是活跃的研究问题，使用时需要谨慎</li>\n<li>高风险决策场景应优先选择事前可解释模型，中低风险场景可使用黑箱模型+事后解释</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"可解释 AI","id":"可解释-ai"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念","id":"核心概念"},{"level":2,"text":"SHAP 值解释框架","id":"shap-值解释框架"},{"level":2,"text":"LIME 与反事实解释","id":"lime-与反事实解释"},{"level":2,"text":"可解释性与性能的权衡","id":"可解释性与性能的权衡"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"}],"prev":{"title":"AI 治理框架","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/data-ethics-privacy/responsible-ai/ai-governance-framework"},"next":{"title":"AI 安全与对齐基础","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/data-ethics-privacy/responsible-ai/ai-safety-alignment"}}